WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.720 --> 00:00:07.280
"Doctor Strange in the Multiverse of Madness" is&nbsp;
finally here, and it's a way different movie than&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.280 --> 00:00:12.000
people were expecting. For one thing, Doctor&nbsp;
Strange doesn’t feel like the main character&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:18.240
here – so who is? Warning: spoilers ahead.
At this point, savvy fans of the MCU know&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:22.720
not to take trailers seriously. Studios&nbsp;
don't want audiences to figure out the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.720 --> 00:00:27.920
movies in advance, so filling trailers up&nbsp;
with fakeouts has become a common practice.&nbsp;

00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:32.480
From editing characters out of scenes to using&nbsp;
dialogue or shots that don't even make it into&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.480 --> 00:00:37.600
the final theatrical cut — the people who market&nbsp;
these movies will do just about anything to lie&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:42.800
to fans about how the actual film takes shape.
The same has once again proven true for Marvel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.800 --> 00:00:48.560
Studios' latest theatrical release: "Doctor&nbsp;
Strange in the Multiverse of Madness." Here's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.560 --> 00:00:53.280
every time the trailers lied to us.
"We should tell him the truth."

00:00:54.640 --> 00:00:59.680
The teaser and official trailer for "Doctor&nbsp;
Strange in the Multiverse of Madness"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.680 --> 00:01:05.440
strongly imply that the events of the movie occur&nbsp;
as a result of Doctor Strange's spell gone wrong&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.440 --> 00:01:10.480
from "Spider-Man: No Way Home," or that Strange&nbsp;
might attempt another spell that shatters the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.480 --> 00:01:15.680
border between realities in his solo movie.
This proved to be a total misdirect,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.680 --> 00:01:20.400
since the inciting incident for this film&nbsp;
isn't a Doctor Strange spell of any kind!&nbsp;

00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:25.040
Marvel Studios executive Kevin Feige noted at&nbsp;
the film's world premiere, the final episode of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.040 --> 00:01:31.200
"Loki" provides the singular event that makes the&nbsp;
problems in the multiverse possible. If anything,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.200 --> 00:01:36.400
Wanda meddles more in the multiverse to&nbsp;
start the movie than Strange himself, as she&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.400 --> 00:01:40.800
desperately searches for a way into a universe&nbsp;
where she can live in peace with her children.&nbsp;

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:45.520
The film's teaser trailer uses lines from the&nbsp;
most recent "Spider-Man" movie to imply that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.520 --> 00:01:50.880
this film's events result from all the different&nbsp;
Spider-Man characters crashing into Earth-616.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.880 --> 00:01:57.040
Again, that's not the case. Strange only gets&nbsp;
involved after America Chavez falls right into&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.040 --> 00:02:02.400
his lap with a dead alternate version of himself&nbsp;
and a monster sent by Wanda in hot pursuit.&nbsp;

00:02:02.400 --> 00:02:08.320
The first "Doctor Strange" movie distinctly&nbsp;
sets up Karl Mordo as Strange's main adversary&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.320 --> 00:02:13.760
after Dormammu and Kaecilius are defeated.
Mordo, of course, does appear in "Doctor&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.760 --> 00:02:19.360
Strange in the Multiverse of Madness" — but not&nbsp;
at all in the way fans expected. Without context,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.360 --> 00:02:24.240
trailers for the movie certainly make it&nbsp;
seem as if Strange causes irreparable harm&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.240 --> 00:02:29.680
to the main MCU universe, inciting Mordo&nbsp;
to re-emerge and punish his ex-friend&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.680 --> 00:02:35.520
for the so-called desecration of reality.
In the finished movie, Strange only meets Mordo&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.520 --> 00:02:41.280
again after traveling to Earth-838 with America&nbsp;
and seeking out that universe's Sorcerer Supreme:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.280 --> 00:02:46.320
Mordo, who works with the Illuminati.&nbsp;
The Illuminati explain to Strange that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.320 --> 00:02:51.520
they killed their universe's version of Strange&nbsp;
after the defeat of Thanos because he was such a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.520 --> 00:02:56.640
liability for the stability of the multiverse.
While the Illuminati's emergence makes for an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.640 --> 00:03:01.840
interesting sequence, Strange and America&nbsp;
spend little time with them. Wanda tears the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.840 --> 00:03:07.600
Illuminati — Charles Xavier and Reed Richards&nbsp;
included — to shreds with relative ease. All in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.600 --> 00:03:12.480
all, Patrick Stewart's screen time in the movie&nbsp;
is barely longer than the trailers themselves.&nbsp;

00:03:13.200 --> 00:03:16.480
"That doesn't seem fair."
Aside from Strange and Wanda,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.480 --> 00:03:21.840
America Chavez may receive the third-most amount&nbsp;
of screen time of any character by the end of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.840 --> 00:03:27.120
the film's 126-minute runtime. Audiences may&nbsp;
not have guessed that from trailers, though;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.120 --> 00:03:32.320
America is largely seen in the background.
Of course, Marvel Studios and Disney likely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.320 --> 00:03:36.800
had their reasons for holding back this&nbsp;
brand-new character: America's powers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:36.800 --> 00:03:42.160
and the details of how she meets Strange and&nbsp;
Wong in the first place, are spoiler-heavy.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.160 --> 00:03:47.440
Additionally, this movie is America's initiation&nbsp;
to the MCU. Casual moviegoers catching the trailer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.440 --> 00:03:53.280
probably don't even recognize the character.
Even so, America makes for a dominating force&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:53.280 --> 00:03:58.400
in the movie as her powers make her the only known&nbsp;
person across the multiverse capable of shifting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:58.400 --> 00:04:04.720
herself between realms. Wanda and Strange both&nbsp;
use the Darkhold to dreamwalk in other universes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:04.720 --> 00:04:09.760
through other versions of themselves, but they&nbsp;
need America with them to make a physical leap.&nbsp;

00:04:09.760 --> 00:04:13.760
By the film's end, America takes control&nbsp;
of her multiverse-hopping abilities,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:13.760 --> 00:04:19.120
and even finds a temporary home at Kamar-Taj&nbsp;
in Earth-616. The character seems like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:19.120 --> 00:04:24.320
an important one, who will likely play a&nbsp;
significant role in MCU projects to come.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:24.320 --> 00:04:29.120
You wouldn't know it by the trailers, though.
